{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 55,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the choirmaster. With stringed instruments. A Maskil of David. Listen to my prayer, O God, and do not ignore my plea.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Attend to me and answer me. I am restless in my complaint, and distraught",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "at the voice of the enemy, at the pressure of the wicked. For they bring down disaster upon me and resent me in their anger.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My heart pounds within me, and the terrors of death assail me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fear and trembling grip me, and horror has overwhelmed me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I said, “Oh, that I had wings like a dove! I would fly away and find rest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How far away I would flee! In the wilderness I would remain. Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I would hurry to my shelter, far from this raging tempest.”",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O Lord, confuse and confound their speech, for I see violence and strife in the city.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Day and night they encircle the walls, while malice and trouble lie within.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Destruction is within; oppression and deceit never leave the streets.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For it is not an enemy who insults me; that I could endure. It is not a foe who rises against me; from him I could hide.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But it is you, a man like myself, my companion and close friend.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We shared sweet fellowship together; we walked with the crowd into the house of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let death seize them by surprise; let them go down to Sheol alive, for evil is with them in their homes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I call to God, and the LORD saves me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Morning, noon, and night, I cry out in distress, and He hears my voice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He redeems my soul in peace from the battle waged against me, even though many oppose me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God will hear and humiliate them — the One enthroned for the ages — Selah because they do not change and they have no fear of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My companion attacks his friends; he violates his covenant.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His speech is smooth as butter, but war is in his heart. His words are softer than oil, yet they are swords unsheathed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Cast your burden upon the LORD and He will sustain you; He will never let the righteous be shaken.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.55.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But You, O God, will bring them down to the Pit of destruction; men of bloodshed and deceit will not live out half their days. But I will trust in You.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
